Hello Ada,

This message is encoded as UTF-7, which almost nothing sends any more
but which IMAP still uses for mailbox names. The next line is the
interesting part:

  M+APg-ller, Gr+APwA3w-e, +ZeVnLIqe, and a literal plus sign: +-

If a decoder mishandles UTF-7 it usually produces the raw +-AOk- style
escapes instead of letters, which is exactly the failure worth testing.

